values ('c1a7e4d8-2b59-4f06-9c31-5e0d8a6b7f14', 'food-science', 'Food Science', 'This course examines how food composition, molecular structure, physical properties, microorganisms, processing, packaging, and storage determine safety, nutritional quality, sensory properties, functionality, and shelf life. Students study water, carbohydrates, proteins, enzymes, lipids, micronutrients, pigments, flavors, colloids, rheology, additives, thermal and nonthermal processing, fermentation, preservation, packaging, sensory science, quality assurance, regulation, and sustainability. Laboratory work emphasizes safe technique, standardized preparation, analytical measurement, experimental design, statistics, scientific writing, and an evidence-based product-development project relevant to nutrition and dietetics.');

